  "measurement_note": "Size S is the subset-space size 2^n. Near-complete graphs with n = 3, 5, and 7 give sizes 8, 32, and 128 across a 16x span. Labels contain n - 2 copies of a plus one b and one c, creating three odd counts so no full-length palindrome exists. The accepted DP memoizes mask/endpoints; a correct exhaustive simple-path search grows factorially and must fail only scaling.",
